; 104:6-9; 107:25-29; Isa 50:2; Jer 5:22; Na 1:4 and rebuked.As the agitation of the sea was merely the effect of the wind, it was necessary to remove the cause of the commotion before the effect would cease. But who, by simply saying Peace, be still, (Mr 4:39,) could do this but God? One word of our Lord can change the face of nature, and calm the troubled ocean, as well as restore peace to the disconsolate soul.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-25","title":"Luke 8:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Where. 12:28; Mt 6:30; 8:26; 14:31; 17:20; Mr 4:40,41; Joh 11:40 being. Ge 1:9,10; Jos 10:12-14; Job 38:8-10; Pr 8:29; 30:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-26","title":"Luke 8:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Mt 8:28-34 Gergesenes. Mr 5:1-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-27","title":"Luke 8:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>met. Mr 5:2-5 and ware. 1Sa 19:24 but. Nu 19:16; Isa 65:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-28","title":"Luke 8:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>he cried. 4:33-36; Mt 8:29; Mr 1:24-27; 5:6-8; Ac 16:16-18 What. 37,38 I beseech. Isa 27:1; 2Pe 2:4; 1Jo 3:8; Jas 2:19; Re 20:1-3,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-29","title":"Luke 8:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>commanded. Mr 5:8; Ac 19:12-16 caught. 9:39,42; Mr 5:3-5; 9:20-26; 2Ti 2:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-30","title":"Luke 8:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Legion. Mt 26:53; Mr 5:9 many. 2; Mt 8:29; Mr 16:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-31","title":"Luke 8:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>they. 28; Job 1:11; 2:5; Php 2:10,11 the deep.\"The abyss,\" says Dr. Doddridge, \"the prison in which many of these fallen spirits are detained; and to which some, who may, like these, have been permitted for a while to range at large, are sometimes by Divine justice and power remanded.\"</p>\n<p>Mt 25:41; Re 9:2; 19:20; 20:2,3,14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-32","title":"Luke 8:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>there an. Le 11:7; Isa 65:4; 66:3; Mt 8:30-33; Mr 5:11-13 besought. Job 1:10; Ps 62:11; Joh 19:11; 1Jo 4:4 he suffered. 1Ki 22:22; Job 1:12; 2:6; Re 20:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-33","title":"Luke 8:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>Then.By this was fully evinced the sovereign power of our Lord, and the reality of diabolical agency; \"for,\" says Dr. Doddridge, \"it was self-evident that a herd of swine could not be confederates in any fraud; their death, therefore, in this instructive circumstance, was ten thousand times a greater blessing to mankind than if they had been slain for food, as was intended.\"</p>\n<p>the herd. Joh 8:44; 1Pe 5:8; Re 9:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-34","title":"Luke 8:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>they fled. Mt 8:33; 28:11; Mr 5:14; Ac 19:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-35","title":"Luke 8:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>and found. Isa 49:24,25; 53:12; Heb 2:14,15; 1Jo 3:8 sitting. 2:46; 10:39; Mr 5:15; Ac 22:3 clothed. 27; 15:17 in his. Ps 51:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-37","title":"Luke 8:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>besought. 28; 5:8; De 5:25; 1Sa 6:20; 2Sa 6:8,9; 1Ki 17:18; Job 21:14,15 Mt 8:34; Mr 5:17; Ac 16:39 and he. 9:5,56; 10:10,11,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-38","title":"Luke 8:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>besought. 28,37; De 10:20,21; Ps 27:4; 32:7; 116:12,16; Mr 5:18; Php 1:23 saying. Ex 12:25-27; 13:8,9,14-16; Ps 71:17,18; 78:3-6; 107:21,22,31,32 Ps 111:2-4; 145:3-12; Isa 63:7-13; Mr 5:19,20; Ac 9:13-16 Ga 1:23,24; 1Ti 1:13-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-39","title":"Luke 8:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>Return. 1Ti 5:8 and published. 17:15-18; De 10:21; Ps 66:16; 126:2,3; Da 4:1-3,34-37; Mr 1:45 Joh 4:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-40","title":"Luke 8:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>that. Mt 9:1; Mr 5:21 the people. 5:1; 19:6,37,38,48; Mr 6:20; 12:37; Joh 5:35 waiting. Pr 8:34; Ac 10:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-41","title":"Luke 8:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>there. Mt 9:18-25; Mr 5:22-43 a ruler. 13:14; Ac 13:15; 18:8,17 and he fell. 5:8; 17:16; Re 5:8 and besought. Mt 8:7,8; Mr 5:23; Joh 4:46-49; 11:21; Ac 9:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-42","title":"Luke 8:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>one. 7:12; Ge 44:20-22; Job 1:18,19; Zec 12:10 and she. Job 4:20; Ps 90:5-8; 103:15,16; Ec 6:12; Eze 24:16,25; Ro 5:12 But. 45; Mr 5:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-43","title":"Luke 