rseStart":55,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":55},"content":"<p>her spirit.This expression, thus used of one who had been dead, strongly implies, that at death the soul not only exists separately, but returns and is re-united to the body, when it is raised from the dead.</p>\n<p>1Ki 17:21-23; Joh 11:44 and he. 24:41-43; Mr 5:43; Joh 11:44</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-8-56","title":"Luke 8:56","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":56,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":56},"content":"<p>he charged. 5:14; Mt 8:4; 9:30; Mr 5:42,43</p>"}]}